70.m:
This greatness of Indradyumna has been related by me;
all that is wondrous, the secret Puruṣottama, has been declared,
ancient, supremely esoteric, auspicious, and delivering from cyclical existence.

72.m:
At the festival of the gods, the Unborn [Brahmā], upon looking at his mother's toe,
incurred the state of being fallen through sin;
the compassionate Father gave him the holy Gaṅgā, stationed in a meritorious water-pot, which purifies through mere remembrance.

73.m:
Brahmā said:
Saying 'So be it', the hosts of gods departed for heaven;
and the Blessed One, the lord of the gods, entered the womb of Aditi.
